menu "esp-xip-modules BLE (xip_ble)"

    config XIP_BLE
        bool "BLE component (advertising, scan, CoC channel, bonds, wake/sleep modes)"
        depends on BT_ENABLED && BT_NIMBLE_ENABLED
        default n
        help
            Builds a thin subset of NimBLE (advertising with the caller's data, scan with the caller's filters, one LE CoC channel, bonds, wake/sleep
            modes) and offers get_component("nimble"). The policy is the caller's (modules/mod_ble hosts the `ble` component, 104). Off: the component is a stub that offers
            nothing and links no Bluetooth code. Also set CONFIG_BT_ENABLED=n to leave the controller and the host out of the image
            (profiles/off.defaults); the options of the NimBLE stack itself (roles, connections, bonds, buffers) are the bt component's and are
            set with the profile files in components/xip_ble/profiles (README.md has the measured table).

    config XIP_BLE_COC
        bool "LE CoC channel (listen, connect, bearer)"
        depends on XIP_BLE
        default y
        help
            One L2CAP connection-oriented channel with a single-record transmit buffer. Needs CONFIG_BT_NIMBLE_L2CAP_COC_MAX_NUM >= 1.
            Off: advertising, scan and bonds only.

    config XIP_BLE_COC_MTU
        int "Largest CoC SDU size a module may ask for, bytes"
        depends on XIP_BLE_COC
        range 256 1500
        default 1500
        help
            The limit, and the MTU of the runtime link "ble". The module that starts the stack chooses the SDU size of the channel (nimble.start: coc_mtu) and the
            pool is allocated with it then, not at build time. One QUIC packet is one SDU. 1500 is XIP_PKT_MAX, the payload of every pool packet and of the ESP-NOW link; quic-lite's own limit is 1100 today.
            The receive copy is on the NimBLE host task stack, so this also bounds that stack use.

    config XIP_BLE_COC_BUFS
        int "Most CoC buffers a module may ask for (one SDU each)"
        depends on XIP_BLE_COC
        range 3 8
        default 3
        help
            One channel needs the receive buffer posted to NimBLE, the received SDU while it is copied into a pool packet, and the transmit mbuf: 3, which
            is also the least nimble.start accepts. The module chooses the count (coc_buffers) when it starts the stack. The connect request's buffer becomes
            the receive buffer, so it is not an extra one.

    config XIP_BLE_SCAN_CACHE
        int "Scan cache entries (distinct advertisers kept for ble.scan_results)"
        depends on XIP_BLE
        range 0 16
        default 8
        help
            9 bytes each, static. 0 builds the cache out (scan results are then only counted, with the last one in the status).

    config XIP_BLE_LOG_LEVEL
        int "Log lines of the BLE mechanics (0 none, 1 failures, 2 all)"
        depends on XIP_BLE
        range 0 2
        default 2
        help
            The lines are the former "event type=ble.*" records. Level 0 removes the strings and the formatting from the image.

    config XIP_BLE_RELEASE_WHEN_OFF
        bool "Release the BLE controller memory when the application boots with BLE off"
        depends on XIP_BLE
        default n
        help
            xip_ble_configure_boot(false) calls esp_bt_mem_release(): the controller's static memory returns to the heap for this boot,
            and BLE cannot start until the next reboot with the boot flag on. Leave it off when BLE may be started later by a request.

endmenu
